  "problem": "If $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10$ and $h(10)=15,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10))=$\n {{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Since $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)=h(10)=15.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10)) & ={lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}x\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)-5\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(10) \\\\  & =10\\cdot 15-5\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =150-75 \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
